    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="1071" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.01/202</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 17.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3020</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to this Embassy’s despatch No.
                    2382, January 9, 1928,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d929-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy, in triplicate, of an informal note received today from
                    the Foreign Office in reply to Mr. Atherton’s<anchor n="21" xml:id="d929-f2"/>
                    informal note to Mr. Oliphant<anchor n="22" xml:id="d929-f3"/> of January 4,
                        1928.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d929-f4"/></p>
                <p>It will be observed that the British Government and the Government of Iraq agree
                    to all of the amendments which the Department wished to make in the proposed
                    Convention between the United Kingdom, the United States and Iraq, with one
                    exception; namely, the proposed alteration in the wording of Article 4, dealing
                    with the position of educational, philanthropic and religious institutions.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to request the Department’s instructions in regard to this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. L.
                        Belin</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">First Secretary of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d929-a1.xml" xpointer="d929-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
